  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a differentiable function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Then,"
  },
  "options": [
